T OutlinerPanel                   | OutlinerPanel.h | 39-105 | owning                        | -  | The presentation half of `12` — reads the linearisation, declares intent, stores neither relation. Only the counted span the artist can see is touched, and the scroll position is a row ordinal resolved by count rather than a pixel offset the panel remembers on its own. A panel that mutated the relations where the click arrived would apply against a linearisation that is halfway rebuilt, and would bypass the sequence that undoes it. entry, and whether the panel is shown. None of it is a transaction and none of it is scrubbed.
